# GitHub Issue Labels

Use this label set when triaging, creating, or updating issues in https://github.com/gambitph/Start-Stackable

Priority, release target, and status belong on the [release project board](https://github.com/orgs/gambitph/projects/2/views/1), not labels.

## Type (exactly one)

| Label | Use for |
|-------|---------|
| `bug` | Something broken in the current release |
| `enhancement` | Improvement to an existing feature |
| `feature-request` | New header, footer, canvas, token, or workflow |
| `question` | How-to, support, or unclear reports |
| `documentation` | Docs, readme, or in-theme help |

## Triage (zero or one, temporary)

| Label | Use for |
|-------|---------|
| `needs-reproduction` | Cannot verify; waiting on repro steps |
| `might-be-fixed` | Likely fixed; checking changelog or codebase |
| `not-planned` | Valid request, explicitly out of scope |
| `duplicate` | Same as another issue |
| `invalid` | Not actionable |
| `wontfix` | Will not be addressed |

Remove triage labels when closing or confirming status.

## Area (zero or one)

| Label | Use for |
|-------|---------|
| `chrome` | Header, footer, sticky/transparent/hide flags |
| `tokens` | `theme.json`, style variations, widths, spacing |
| `templates` | Templates, parts, patterns, page canvases |
| `onboarding` | Recommend-plugin notice, first-run |
| `compatibility` | WordPress, Site Editor, plugin snap-in |
| `accessibility` | a11y |
| `frontend` | Saved markup, CSS, or JS on the site |
| `performance` | Speed, asset size |
| `theme-review` | WordPress.org Theme Directory constraints |

## Community (optional)

| Label | Use for |
|-------|---------|
| `good first issue` | Good for new contributors |
| `help wanted` | Extra attention welcome |

## Pull requests

| Label | Use for |
|-------|---------|
| `pr: needs review` | Awaiting review |
| `pr: reviewed` | Reviewed with comments |
| `pr: good to merge` | Approved |

## Rules

- Apply **one type** label per issue.
- Apply **at most one** triage label and **at most one** area label.
- Do **not** use priority or version labels.
